This is an example of a self-indicting acknowledgment that contains no change of behavior. The moral pivot works precisely because Annie's accountability sounds real. It generates enough emotional relief — 'she admitted it, she knows, maybe now things will change' — to reset Dan's demand for actual change back to zero. Thirteen major apologies are documented in the record. Thirteen. Each one was followed by identical behavior.

